---
title: Thai Peanut Noodles
description: Rice noodles and chopped chicken thighs tossed in a creamy peanut-soy-lime sauce, finished with peanuts and herbs.
source: https://tornadoughalli.com/thai-peanut-noodles/
author: Tornadough Alli
changes:
  - Add 2 lb chopped boneless skinless chicken thighs
  - Triple the sauce (peanut butter, soy, lime, brown sugar, sesame oil, chili paste, and thinning liquid)
  - Make the sauce in a pot instead of a saucepan
servings: 6
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
time required: 35 minutes
course: main
cuisine: Thai-inspired
tags:
  - noodles
  - peanut
  - chicken
  - quick
  - scaling
---

Cook @rice noodles{6%oz}(about a 6–6.3 oz package; lo mein or fettuccine also work if you skip rinsing) in boiling water according to package directions until tender, about ~{5-6%minutes}. Reserve @pasta water{6%tbsp}, then drain, rinse, and toss in a #large bowl{} with @sesame oil{1%tbsp}. Set aside.

Meanwhile, heat @vegetable oil{1%tbsp} in a #large skillet{} over medium-high heat. Add @boneless skinless chicken thighs{2%lb}(chopped) and cook, stirring occasionally, until golden and an instant-read thermometer reads 165°F, about ~{10-12%minutes}. Season with @kosher salt{} and @black pepper{}. Transfer to the bowl with the noodles.

In a #pot{} over medium-low heat, whisk @creamy peanut butter{1%cup}, @soy sauce{9%tbsp}, @lime juice{6%tbsp}(fresh), @brown sugar{6%tbsp}, remaining @sesame oil{3%tbsp}, and @chili paste{3%tsp} until smooth, about ~{2%minutes}.

Whisk in the reserved warm pasta water (or @coconut milk{6%tbsp} for a creamier sauce) to thin slightly; remove from heat.

Add the sauce to the noodles and chicken and toss until completely coated. Top with @roasted peanuts{2%tbsp}(unsalted, chopped), @scallions{2%tbsp}(sliced), and @fresh cilantro{}(chopped). Serve immediately.
